    "metric_supported_solution": "K=2 is the mathematically optimal clustering solution, yielding highest Silhouette score (0.4060), lowest Davies-Bouldin index (1.0990), highest Calinski-Harabasz score (1154.38), and 100% stability across multiple random initializations. It cleanly separates smooth, low-perimeter tissue (Cluster 1) from textured, high-perimeter foliar surfaces (Cluster 0).",
